From dd8f6d06b3db03048b0670cb81e00a8af12b0b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 05:34:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] circsim+editor: animate the S/W switch blade with the run's
 answer

- symbols: SwitchBlade (pivot + open/closed tips) on the s/w table
  entries - the moving contact leaves the static draw list; .csym
  round-trips "blade" {pivot/open/closed} (a malformed one drops to
  the static picture); symbol_bounds grows both endpoints so the
  swing never leaves the AABB
- render: render_symbol(sym, placement, switch_closed = 0.0) draws
  the blade interpolated - endpoints verbatim (t=0 bit-identical to
  the old static line), the angle's shortest rotational path + the
  radius between, interpolated in LOCAL space under the shared
  transform; every static consumer (SVG dump, PNG, palette, ghost)
  keeps the open rest
- overlay: overlay_switch - the SW device's exact hysteresis walk
  (devices_m2's law, initial open) over the control column from row
  0 to the playhead's sample: v(c+) - v(c-) for an S (pins through
  the run's own net build, ground pins read 0 V), i(<vs>) for a W
  (the deck's spelling, resolved case-insensitively when the param's
  differs); thresholds from the model the part names - the
  directives' .model card first (export's resolution order), else
  the built-in library - parsed with ws::spice's own deck reader
  (continuations and glued parens read as the run read them)
- editor: the canvas eases the blade ~120 ms toward the walk's
  answer, the LED glow's own tempo (instant with the theme's motion
  off, resting open with no run or no answer)
- tests: the blade's table entry + the .csym round-trip + the broken
  blade's drop, the render interpolation (mirror riding the moving
  tip), the walk's hysteresis band/threshold precedence/spelling
  tolerance/W-current/.op cases, and the editor's .dc-swept blade
  case (open before the run, thrown at the sweep's end, back open at
  its start)
